    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Immunotx: nivolumab plus ipilimumab = typically preferred; nivolumab plus relatlimab (LAG-3) = an alt w better tolerability; a PD-1 inhibitor alone = also an option. Neoadjuvant PD-1 inhibitors are recommended for selected pts"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "BRAF-mutant, Sxtomatic or rapidly progress dz: BRAF plus MEK inhibitors (dabrafenib/trametinib, encorafenib/binimetinib, vemurafenib/cobimetinib) may be preferred for faster response"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "T-VEC (intralesional oncolytic herpesvirus) may be considered for unresectable metastatic melanoma; cytotoxic chemo hasn't improved survival and = kept for pts w ⍉other options"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
